### Gameplay & Interaction

Every Sudoku puzzle is generated with a unique solution, so you'll never get an ambiguous grid.

- **Puzzle generation** — The code fills a full 9×9 grid using backtracking, then removes cells while checking that the resulting puzzle still has exactly one solution. It keeps 34 clues by default.
- **Controls** — Click any cell to select it, then enter a digit 1–9 using the on-screen pad or your keyboard. Press Backspace, Delete, or 0 to clear the cell. Arrow keys move the selection.
- **Visual feedback** — The selected cell is outlined in blue. Matching digits in the same row, column, or 3×3 box are highlighted. Incorrect or conflicting entries turn red and show a lighter red background.
- **Win condition** — The status bar shows the number of empty cells. When the grid is filled correctly, it displays the message "🎉 Complimenti! Sudoku completato!".
- **New game** — The "Nuova partita" button generates a fresh puzzle with a new solution, resetting the board and any highlights.
---

**Optimization Tip:** To make the puzzle easier or harder, adjust the number in `generatePuzzle(34)` near the bottom of the script — lower values like 30 give more empty cells, higher values like 40 give fewer. The uniqueness check will still remove cells only if the puzzle remains solvable.

